1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''Sigurd, husb of Gyrid* INGEMUNDSDATTER''' was born about 1290 in Norway. He died before 1362 in Norway. The only mention of Sigurd is in a document from 1362. His patronymic was not mentioned in this document a
2 CONC nd it is unknown where he lived. He was married to Gyrid* INGEMUNDSDATTER in Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Gyrid INGEMUNDSDATTER''' was born about 1300 in Skjervheim gård #138, Vats, Rogaland, Norway. She died after 1362 in Norway. Gyrid Ingemundsdatter was a member of the wealthy and powerful Ingemund family. In 1362, she appeared
2 CONC  in court with her daughter to claim ownership of the Frøyland farm. Gyrid claimed that the farm had been given to her by a cousin, Sira (priest) Eimund Ogmundsson. Gyrid had two sworn witnesses that confirmed she had received it 
2 CONC from Sira Eimund. She won the case and Frøyland remained in the family until 1405 when her daughter, Sigrid, who was married to Jon Tollaksson, sold Frøyland (DN 4 nr 748). Children were: '''Siri* SIGURDSDATTER''' Frøyland.
