2 CONT <p>Lund, Skår 259.III og Ætt&Heim 1956 s.108.</p><p><p>Sønn av Arnbjørn Ogmundson Byre, Hardanger. Nevnt 1346.</p></p><p>Sønn eller svigersønn: Arne.</p>
2 CONT
2 CONT AI:
2 CONT Ogmund Arnbjørnsen Aga, also known as Amund Arnbjørnsen Skartveit, was a notable figure in medieval Norway. Here are some key details about him:
2 CONT
2 CONT Background and Family
2 CONT Birth and Death: Ogmund was born around 1335 in Byre, Finnøy, Rogaland, Norway, and he died in 14361.
2 CONT Family: He was the son of Arnbjørn Ogmundsson and Magnhild Kjetilsdatter1. Ogmund married Sigrid Arnesdatter Aga, and they had children, including Eivind Ogmundson1.
2 CONT Roles and Contributions
2 CONT Landowner: Ogmund was a significant landowner in the Hardanger region. He owned properties in both Byre and Aga1.
2 CONT Historical Mentions: He is mentioned in various historical documents from around 1360, indicating his active role in the local governance and society1.
2 CONT Legacy
2 CONT Influence: Ogmund’s family, the Aga family, held considerable influence in the region, contributing to the local governance and aristocracy of medieval Norway1.
