2 CONT Title: The Sloopers: Their Ancestry and Posterity 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Peder var først gift med Sissel Olavsdtr, Håland, født omkring 1597. De hadde 5 barn i sammen i 1. ekteskap: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) Orm Perderson, Hovda i Fister, f. 1610. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2) Olav Pederson, Foss, skifte 04.11.1691, gift med Kari Oddsdtr, trolig fra Haua. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3) Tormod Pederson, Kalseim, f. 1615. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4) Anna Pedersdtr, Høyland.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5) Guri Pedersdtr, f. 1620, gift med Ola Nilsson, Landsnes.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT I 1610 var han bøndenes representant ved kongehyllingen i Oslo. (Slektene Velde og Espeland og inngiftede slekter. s. 146.)
2 CONT Han hadde halve gården på Foss, Hjelmeland fra 1603 til 1670. I årene 1648-1654 drev sønnen Orm sammen med ham.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Peder Tormodsson farmed at Foss for 67 years and was a wealthy
2 CONT landowner of 4 laup smør for many years.  He operated 2 laupar smør
2 CONT at Foss between 1603 and 1627. From 1627 until 1660, he operated the
2 CONT entire farm (4 laupar smør), of which he owned half.  After 1660,
2 CONT Peder had 1/3 of the farm and two of his sons operated the remainder.
2 CONT He owned a quarter of Kjølvik sawmill in Jelsa.  Peder, along with his
2 CONT sons, also reclaimed the deserted farm Nesvik and put it back into
2 CONT operation.
2 CONT Peder is often mentioned in the local records.  The first time was in
2 CONT in 1601, when he claimed his share of his deceased brother's estate.
2 CONT In 1603, he was named as one of the few farmers who owned at least 3
2 CONT laupar smør.  In 1610, he was elected to represent Hjelmeland at the
2 CONT royal coronation in Oslo.  Peder sued Jens Kjølvik on 18 Dec 1619 over
2 CONT the right to use Kjølvik sawmill.  Peder produced a document showing
2 CONT that he had legally obtained these rights and won the case.
2 CONT In 1632, Peder sued Knut Sigmundstad over some pigs that had been
2 CONT killed by a boar while in Knut's care.  The case was postponed and the
2 CONT outcome is unknown.
2 CONT On 3 Jun 1668, Peder divided his personal property among his children.
2 CONT His estate was probated in 1670 and 5 laupar 29 mark smør was divided
2 CONT among his heirs.  This included property at Kalsheim, Førre, Fossåen
2 CONT and Ravnsfjeld.  It appears that he must have previously sold his 2
2 CONT laupar smør at Foss.
