2 ADDR
3 CITY 4120 Tau
3 STAE Rogaland
3 CTRY Norge
1 OCCU bonde, Bonde
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Knut leased probably the farm at Høyland from 1674.  He did not conduct
2 CONT military service.  He grew up at Øvre Bjørheim and moved undoubtedly to
2 CONT Høyland together with his mother.  Knut purchased 0.5 "pund smør" at Øvre
2 CONT Bjørheim in 1674.  The sellers were Hans Knutson and Laurits Olson Nerhus.
2 CONT He was a juror in 1678.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1679 Anna Høyland and her son Knut summoned witnesses to court who
2 CONT testified that that their farm with all its 9 houses and buildings had
2 CONT burned down during the night after St. Hans in the summer of 1679.  They were
2 CONT therefore left as poor people in great poverty.
2 CONT
2 CONT From the customs list for Stavanger it prevails that Knut made two trips to
2 CONT Stavanger in October 1681.  The first time he brought with him one head of
2 CONT cattle and one barrel of nuts, and on his second trip there were 3 barrels
2 CONT of nuts and one pig in his boat.  On 8 December 1682 Knut brought with him
2 CONT 2.5 barrels of nuts to town.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1681 Knut Olson Høyland had registered a letter of purchase of 2.5 "pund
2 CONT smør" at Høyland.  This land he had bought from his uncle Jon Torson, and
2 CONT Ola Kjølevik, whos was married to his aunt.  Knut would himself live on the
2 CONT land.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1682 Knut Olson Høyland had also registered a letter of purchase of
2 CONT 1 "pund" and 4 "merker smør" at Høyland.  This land he had bought from
2 CONT Tore Torson (also a brother of his father) whos lived at Tysvær, Tysvær.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1694 Knut Høyland summoned Knut Øvre Bjørheim to court because he owed
2 CONT "Hans Moder, Anna Endresdtr" 8 "riksdalar", which was the remaining amount
2 CONT for the land on which Knut Øvre Bjørheim then lived.
2 CONT
2 CONT And in 1699 it is stated: "Knud Olsen Høyland lod oplæse oc tinglyse en
2 CONT forligelse som i mellom hans søskende er gjort, i det Knud skal lade
2 CONT begrafue sin gammel Moder Anna Endresdatter Som er hos ham, naar hun ved
2 CONT Døden heden kaldes, som hans Moder Anna Endres. sig kand haffue effterlat
2 CONT Naar hun er begrafuet det at til komme Knud Olsen allene."  This Anna
2 CONT presumably died in 1702.
2 CONT
2 CONT Knut operated the entire Høyland farm in 1706.  They had 2 children at home
2 CONT in 1711, and also "i Liden gietle Dreng, Christopher".  In 1723 Knut
2 CONT operated half of the farm.  When his wife, Kari's estate was wound up in
2 CONT 1734, her gross wealth was 118 "riksdalar", and after that liabilities and
2 CONT expenses had been deducted, 82 "riksdalar" were left.
